Page {T 'ACKNOWLEDGEMENT' 1 16 $true 28|Out-Null;T 'I express my sincere gratitude to my project supervisor, faculty members and the Department of [to be inserted] for their guidance and support during the development and documentation of Samay. Their direction helped shape this work into a practical mobile application for focused study and collaborative learning.' 3 12 $false 14|Out-Null;T 'I thank my peers and family for their encouragement. I also acknowledge the open-source communities behind React Native, Expo, Firebase and React Navigation, whose documentation and software form important technical foundations for this implementation.' 3 12 $false 14|Out-Null;T 'Finally, I acknowledge everyone who provided feedback during the project. Any remaining gaps between this report and the final institutional format can be completed when college-specific guidelines and approval details are supplied.' 3 12 $false 0|Out-Null;T 'Sanjay' 2 11 $false 0|Out-Null }
Page {T 'ABSTRACT' 1 16 $true 18|Out-Null;T 'Samay is an Android-oriented mobile study productivity and group collaboration application implemented with React Native, Expo and TypeScript. It combines personal planning with a focus timer, study-session recording, todo planning, calendar views, statistics and a social study-group workspace. Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore provide the authenticated and cloud-backed portions of the implementation, while AsyncStorage maintains selected local preferences and timer recovery state.' 3 11 $false 10|Out-Null;T 'The implementation uses a provider-based application shell, React Navigation for authenticated and unauthenticated routes, focused service modules for Firestore operations and custom hooks for reactive screen state. The group subsystem includes public/private group access, membership requests, member roles, chat, attendance views and leaderboards.' 3 11 $false 10|Out-Null;T 'This report is an evidence-led technical account. It separates source-level validation from runtime claims: the repository includes a TypeScript compilation output, but no supplied evidence demonstrates a live Firebase or multi-device test run. Keywords: React Native, Firebase, focus timer, study productivity, collaboration.' 3 10 $true 0|Out-Null }
