Page {T 'LIST OF ABBREVIATIONS' 1 16 $true 10|Out-Null;Grid @('Term','Meaning') @(@('API','Application Programming Interface'),@('DND','Do Not Disturb'),@('SDK','Software Development Kit'),@('UI/UX','User Interface / User Experience'),@('UID','Firebase Authentication user identifier'),@('CRUD','Create, read, update and delete'),@('TSX','TypeScript syntax for React components'));T 'In this report, implemented means a source-level implementation was inspected. Verified means a supplied artefact directly supports the claim. The distinction avoids converting client code into unsupported runtime claims.' 3 10 $false 0|Out-Null }
Page {H 'CHAPTER 1: INTRODUCTION';H '1.1 Project Background' 2;T 'Independent study combines planned work, uninterrupted focus and peer accountability. Students commonly use separate timer, task, calendar and messaging tools, which fragments the workflow and makes it difficult to associate planned work with completed study time. Samay addresses this context through one mobile application that joins personal productivity functions with group collaboration.';H '1.2 Problem Statement' 2;T 'The project addresses the absence of an integrated workflow that lets an authenticated student plan work, run a focus session, retain session history, inspect progress and participate in a study group without moving among unrelated applications. It records user-driven activity; it does not claim automatic measurement of study quality.';H '1.3 Motivation' 2;T 'A todo is more useful when it can be associated with planned duration and actual focus seconds. Group membership can provide accountability through attendance, activity indicators, chat and leaderboards while keeping individual work in a mobile interface.' }
Page {H '1.4 Objectives' 2;B @('Provide authentication-aware entry and profile routing.','Provide a category-based focus timer with start, pause, resume, stop, cancel and reset paths.','Record study sessions and present recent, daily and weekly information.','Provide todos with planned dates/duration and an 80% automatic completion rule.','Support groups, member roles, chat, attendance and leaderboards.','Maintain selected local preferences and recovery keys with AsyncStorage.');H '1.5 Scope of the Project' 2;T 'The scope is a React Native mobile client configured with an Android native project and Firebase services. It includes screens, hooks, service modules and native Android DND support. CamStudyComingSoonScreen exists in the source; camera study is therefore treated as coming soon, not a delivered feature.';H '1.6 Stakeholders' 2;T 'Learners are the primary users. Group creators/admins manage roles and private-group requests. Firebase is an external managed dependency rather than a backend deployed by this repository.' }
Page {H '1.7 Existing System' 2;T 'A typical arrangement separates timer, task list, calendar and group chat across different tools. This can duplicate entry, disconnect planned tasks from achieved focus time and make group accountability manual. The repository contains no comparative user study or benchmark, so the limitation discussion is conceptual rather than empirical.';H '1.8 Proposed System' 2;T 'Samay uses an authenticated route stack, bottom tabs for Home, Focus, Todo, Calendar and Groups, and additional detail screens. The service layer separates Firestore operations into userProfile.ts, todos.ts, sessions.ts, groups.ts, chat.ts and attendance.ts.';H '1.9 Advantages' 2;B @('One workflow links planning, focus time and reporting.','Firestore snapshot listeners are used for reactive client data.','Private groups have join-request code; public groups have a direct join path.','Core features remain available through bottom tabs.','Screens, services, hooks and types are structurally separated.') }
Page {H '1.10 Organization of the Report' 2;T 'Chapter 1 introduces the project. Chapter 2 records related concepts and the source-supported stack. Chapter 3 documents requirements, architecture, data and navigation. Chapter 4 maps the codebase to implemented modules. Chapter 5 distinguishes available validation evidence from unverified runtime behavior. Chapter 6 concludes the work and identifies future scope.';H '1.11 Method of Documentation' 2;T 'The report was prepared by inspecting the TypeScript/TSX source, package configuration, Android project, logs and image assets. No unavailable college guideline, previous report, Firebase console evidence or device trace was inferred. File names, exported functions, package dependencies and Firestore paths are retained where visible.';H '1.12 Boundary of Claims' 2;T 'This report documents code-level design. It does not claim that sign-in, server reads/writes, security-rule decisions or multi-device synchronization succeeded, because no direct runtime evidence was supplied.' }
Page {H 'CHAPTER 2: LITERATURE REVIEW AND TECHNOLOGY STACK';H '2.1 Related Study / Literature Review' 2;T 'The domain combines personal information management, timeboxing, self-regulated learning and computer-supported collaborative learning. A useful study tool should keep interaction friction low: identify work, begin focus and later interpret the stored record. Group functions should add accountability without replacing the personal workflow.';T 'The references provide conceptual grounding for self-regulation and collaboration. The repository does not include a formal survey dataset, questionnaire or experimental protocol; this review connects established ideas to design decisions without making efficacy claims.';H '2.2 Existing Solutions and Limitations' 2;T 'Separate productivity and communication tools can have strong individual features but disconnected data. Samay explicitly models planned todo duration, actual focus seconds, sessions and group activity. Integration also increases dependence on network availability and backend configuration.' }
Page {H '2.3 Technologies Used' 2;Grid @('Layer','Technology','Use') @(@('Language','TypeScript / TSX','Components, hooks, services and types'),@('Mobile','React Native 0.81.5','Native UI abstraction'),@('Toolkit','Expo ~54.0.33','Runtime/build integration'),@('Navigation','React Navigation','Stacks and tabs'),@('Backend','React Native Firebase','Auth and Firestore'),@('Local storage','AsyncStorage','Preferences and cache'),@('Native','Kotlin / Android','DND bridge'));H '2.4 Programming Languages' 2;T 'The core source is TypeScript/TSX. Kotlin implements the native Android DND bridge. XML is used by Android manifests/resources, and JSON appears in package, Expo and Google-service configuration.' }
Page {H '2.5 Frameworks, Libraries and Backend' 2;T 'React Native provides components; Expo provides application tooling; React Navigation provides stack and tab routing. Firebase Auth supplies current-user state and Firestore provides document, collection, transaction, batch and snapshot operations. React Native SVG and icon packages support visual controls.';H '2.6 Development Tools' 2;T 'The workspace contains Node package metadata, TypeScript configuration and Android Gradle files. build.log, prebuild_output.log, build-error.txt and typecheck-output.txt are evidence artefacts, not guarantees of a clean device build.';H '2.7 Technology Selection' 2;T 'TypeScript declares Todo, FocusSession and Group models. Hooks/contexts support persistent UI state. Firestore maps naturally to user and group subcollections, and AsyncStorage serves selected local state. The trade-off is dependence on backend configuration and rules outside the inspected source.' }
Page {H '2.8 Dependencies and Tool Rationale' 2;Grid @('Package / file','Repository-supported rationale') @(@('@react-native-firebase/auth','Used by useAuth and auth flows'),@('@react-native-firebase/firestore','Collections, batches, transactions and snapshots'),@('@react-native-google-signin/google-signin','Google path in AuthChoiceScreen'),@('@react-navigation/*','Tab and stack routing'),@('AsyncStorage','Terms, avatar, cache and active session keys'),@('expo-image-picker','Declared for profile image selection'),@('react-native-svg','Timer visual support'),@('DNDModule.kt','Android Do Not Disturb bridge'));T 'Versions stated here are declared in package.json. A dependency declaration is not evidence that every runtime path was executed.' 3 10 $false 0|Out-Null }
Page {H 'CHAPTER 3: SYSTEM ANALYSIS AND DESIGN';H '3.1 Functional Requirements' 2;Grid @('ID','Requirement','Evidence') @(@('FR-01','Observe auth state','useAuth.ts'),@('FR-02','Manage user profile','userProfile.ts; Profile screens'),@('FR-03','Run focus timer','useFocusTimer.ts; TimerScreen'),@('FR-04','Manage todos','todos.ts; TodoScreen'),@('FR-05','Track sessions','sessions.ts; Stats/Sessions screens'),@('FR-06','Manage groups','groups.ts; Group screens'),@('FR-07','Group chat','chat.ts; GroupChatScreen'),@('FR-08','Attendance/ranking','attendance.ts; GroupAttendance screens')) }
Page {H '3.2 Non-Functional Requirements' 2;Grid @('Concern','Design response / boundary') @(@('Usability','Five core areas are exposed through tabs.'),@('Responsiveness','Firestore listeners update state after events.'),@('Reliability','Services use error handling, transactions and batches.'),@('Maintainability','Screens, services, hooks, types and context are separated.'),@('Security','UID checks occur in services; final enforcement needs Firestore rules.'),@('Local state','AsyncStorage stores selected state, not full offline sync.'),@('Platform','Android project/DND bridge present; iOS validation absent.'));H '3.3 Hardware and Software Requirements' 2;T 'Development requires Node compatible with package.json (>=20, <23), npm dependencies, Expo/React Native tooling and Android build tools. Runtime requires a mobile device/emulator, network for Firebase paths and valid Firebase/Google configuration. Exact device specification and cloud quota were not verified.' }
Page {H '3.4 System Architecture' 2;T 'The architecture has four layers. Screens present UI and actions. Navigation, contexts and hooks coordinate lifecycle state. Services centralize remote operations. Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore supply cloud identity/documents; AsyncStorage supplements remote data with selected local state.';Fig 'Figure 3.1: System architecture derived from application composition and imports.' @('React Native screens','Navigation, contexts and hooks','Service modules','Firebase Auth / Firestore');T 'App.tsx composes SafeAreaProvider, ThemeProvider and FocusTimerProvider. AppContent reads useAuth, updates online presence and delegates route selection to AppNavigator, confirming a provider-based root composition.' }
Page {H '3.5 Use Case Design' 2;Grid @('Actor','Supported use cases') @(@('Visitor','Authentication choice, email/password flow, reset, Google path'),@('Learner','Profile, dashboard, todos, focus, sessions, calendar, statistics'),@('Group member','Browse group, chat, attendance and rankings'),@('Owner/admin','Create group, manage requests, roles and members'),@('Firebase services','Auth state and cloud document snapshots'));T 'Figure 3.2: Core use-case model represented as an actor/use-case matrix. Client code can request a workflow; Firestore rules ultimately determine server authorization.' 1 10 $false 0|Out-Null }
Page {H '3.6 Data Flow and Authentication Flow' 2;T 'On launch, useAuth registers onAuthStateChanged and onIdTokenChanged. AppNavigator selects AuthStack for a null user. For an authenticated user it checks local terms acceptance, invokes ensureUserProfile for the verified email path, and routes to profile setup or main application. Profile creation reserves a normalized username in a transaction.';Fig 'Figure 3.3: Authentication and profile-routing flow.' @('Launch app','Observe auth state','Sign in / profile checks','Authenticated route tree');T 'This is a client flow. Credential validity and provider exchange depend on Firebase configuration, so successful live authentication is not claimed.' }
Page {H '3.7 Firestore Structure and ER Interpretation' 2;Grid @('Path','Key fields / relationship') @(@('userProfiles/{uid}','username, displayName, email, goals'),@('usernames/{name}','UID reservation'),@('users/{uid}/todos/{id}','title, completion, planned and actual focus'),@('sessions/{id}','UID, timing and optional group context'),@('groups/{id}','group metadata'),@('groups/{id}/members/{uid}','role and study aggregate'),@('groups/{id}/messages/{id}','chat payload'),@('groups/{id}/attendance/{date}/members/{uid}','attendance record'));T 'Figure 3.4: Document/subcollection relationship interpretation. It is not a relational SQL schema and must not be read as a supplied Firestore rules specification.' 1 10 $false 0|Out-Null }
Page {H '3.8 Navigation Architecture' 2;T 'AppNavigator is auth-aware. AuthStack exposes AuthChoice. RootNavigator provides Home, Focus, Todo, Calendar and Groups tabs, plus detail routes such as Leaderboard, CreateGroup, GroupDetail, Profile, GroupChat, Stats and Sessions. AppNavigator additionally includes group administration and attendance routes.';H '3.9 Module Design' 2;Grid @('Module','Principal source files') @(@('Shell','App.tsx; AppNavigator; RootNavigator'),@('Identity','useAuth.ts; userProfile.ts; Profile screens'),@('Focus','useFocusTimer.ts; sessions.ts; TimerScreen'),@('Planning','todos.ts; useCalendarData.ts; Todo/Calendar/Stats'),@('Groups','groups.ts, chat.ts, attendance.ts; Group screens'),@('State/device','storage/services.ts; dnd.ts; ThemeContext.tsx'));T 'Figure 3.5: Navigation and module flow — routes select screens; screens invoke hooks/services; services access storage or Firebase.' 1 10 $false 0|Out-Null }
Page {H 'CHAPTER 4: SYSTEM IMPLEMENTATION';H '4.1 Implementation Overview' 2;T 'The source organization supports a clear implementation narrative. src/screens contains presentation components; src/hooks contains composable state/subscription logic; src/services encapsulates remote operations; src/types declares domain data; and src/context supplies shared theme and focus-timer access. The status statements in this chapter mean that a source implementation was located.';H '4.2 Authentication' 2;T 'useAuth.ts subscribes to Firebase auth state and maintains user/loading state. AuthChoiceScreen.tsx includes Google integration setup, email login and password-reset handlers. AppNavigator.tsx chooses AuthStack for an absent user. This is implemented client logic; successful live sign-in is not evidenced by supplied artefacts.';H '4.3 User Profile' 2;T 'userProfile.ts implements getUserProfile, createInitialUserProfile, ensureUserProfile, availability checks, username change and preference updates. It reserves normalized username documents transactionally.' }
Page {H '4.4 Home Dashboard' 2;T 'HomeScreen.tsx derives an active-todo list, daily progress and recent information, and supplies entry points to focus work. It is a client rendering layer whose values depend on authenticated data and service calls.';H '4.5 Todo Management' 2;T 'todos.ts stores records under users/{uid}/todos. addTodo initializes title, subject, planned duration/start/date, completion and actual-focus fields. updateTodo, deleteTodo and toggleTodo implement CRUD. addFocusSeconds uses a transaction to accumulate duration and marks a todo complete when cumulative focus reaches 80% of planned seconds.';H '4.6 Home-to-Todo Data Flow' 2;T 'Todo subscriptions order records by createdAt. When focus starts for a todo, TimerScreen receives todo/subject/duration route parameters; elapsed time can subsequently be persisted through addFocusSeconds. This links planning to recorded effort.' }
Page {H '4.7 Focus Timer and Study Sessions' 2;T 'FocusTimerProvider exposes useFocusTimer through useFocusTimerContext. The hook defines idle, running and paused states, maintains tick/heartbeat intervals, observes AppState and invokes useAutoDND. Its actions include start, pause, resume, stop, cancel and reset. TimerScreen selects categories, captures an optional target and presents progress.';T 'sessions.ts implements startSession, setStudyingStatus, touchStudyingStatus, cancelSession and completeSession, plus recent/daily/weekly retrieval. completeSession accepts UID, session ID, minutes, seconds and an optional group ID.';Fig 'Figure 4.1: Focus session lifecycle across hook and service.' @('Category + target','Start / heartbeat','Pause or resume','Stop/cancel + persist') }
Page {H '4.8 Calendar' 2;T 'CalendarScreen.tsx and useCalendarData.ts derive daily, weekly and monthly views. The hook computes month boundaries, date keys, session lists and completed todos. The screen supports weekly/monthly display and rescheduling paths such as move-to-tomorrow and move-to-next-week. Local date keys use YYYY-MM-DD formatting.';H '4.9 Statistics and Analytics' 2;T 'StatsScreen.tsx loads recent sessions, today minutes and weekly minutes, then calculates category breakdown, weekly maximum, total week time and average daily time. SessionsScreen provides a detailed historical view. This analysis is derived from stored sessions, not an external analytics service.';H '4.10 Theme and UI State' 2;T 'ThemeContext persists light/dark/system mode with AsyncStorage and exposes DesignSystem tokens. App.tsx also includes an ErrorBoundary for caught rendering errors.' }
Page {H '4.11 Group Creation and Access' 2;T 'groups.ts implements createGroup, getGroup, getGroupsList, joinGroup, leaveGroup and membership checks. createGroup writes group metadata and initial member information through a batch. GroupsListScreen provides browse/sort behavior; CreateGroupScreen captures creation; GroupDetailScreen derives owner/admin permissions.';H '4.12 Public and Private Groups' 2;T 'requestJoinGroup, hasPendingJoinRequest, getPendingJoinRequests, approveJoinRequest and rejectJoinRequest demonstrate a private-group request workflow. The exact Firestore security policy is not inferred because no rules file was supplied.';H '4.13 Roles' 2;T 'Member records are normalized to owner, admin or member. updateGroupMemberRole and removeGroupMember are implemented in groups.ts; GroupMembersScreen and PendingRequestsScreen form associated UI surfaces.' }
Page {H '4.14 Group Chat and Leaderboards' 2;T 'chat.ts defines sendMessage and subscribeToMessages. The send path requires a current authenticated user, trims content and writes a group message. useGroupChat provides hook-facing state and GroupChatScreen renders the view. Supplied screenshots show interface states, but do not prove a live multi-user conversation.';T 'getGroupLeaderboard derives rankings from member data. leaderboard.ts obtains global entries and supplies a subscription. Active group sessions are supported by startActiveFocusSession and stopActiveFocusSession.';Fig 'Figure 4.2: Group collaboration flow.' @('Create / browse','Join or request','Roles and membership','Chat / attendance / rank') }
Page {H '4.15 Attendance Tracking' 2;T 'attendance.ts calculates local date keys and applies ATTENDANCE_THRESHOLD_MINUTES when updating presence. It implements retrieval and subscription helpers for daily, weekly and summary data. GroupAttendance, Champions, Streaks, Weekly, Monthly and MemberAttendance screens expose related views. useGroupAttendance derives present counts, percentages and rankings.';H '4.16 Group Study Aggregation' 2;T 'groups.ts includes updateGroupMemberMinutes. Together with the complete-session optional group identifier and attendance logic, the code offers a route from completed focus work to group measures. The exact runtime call order remains a test requirement.';H '4.17 Online Presence' 2;T 'useOnlinePresence is invoked from AppContent with the current UID and observes application state. It is a source-supported presence mechanism, not proof that another client observed presence.' }
Page {H '4.18 Local Storage and Firebase Integration' 2;T 'storage/services.ts defines keys for terms, welcome banner, local photo, profile cache, active session and pending minutes. consentService, profilePrefsService and userProfileCacheService wrap AsyncStorage. ThemeContext independently stores themeMode. These are continuity mechanisms, not a complete offline synchronization design.';T 'firebase.ts imports native Firebase Auth and Firestore, exposes current UID and helper subscriptions, and exports auth/firestore. android/app/google-services.json is present. Its presence is configuration evidence, not proof of live connectivity.';H '4.19 Do Not Disturb' 2;T 'dnd.ts gates Android support and wraps policy access, enable/disable and settings calls. Native Kotlin source exists in android/app/src/main/java/com/samay/app/dnd. Device permission behavior is unverified.' }
