Page {H '4.24 Security and Privacy Considerations' 2;T 'The client checks for a current UID in several services and separates user-owned paths from group paths. Nevertheless, client checks cannot replace Firestore security rules. No rules file, security audit, data-retention policy or penetration-test artefact was supplied. User profile, todo, session and group content should be protected by reviewed server-side rules before real deployment.';T 'The repository includes PrivacyPolicyScreen, PrivacySecurityScreen, TermsScreen and DeleteAccountScreen, which indicate client UI support for privacy/account journeys. Their legal or backend completion status was not independently verified.' }
Page {H 'CHAPTER 5: TESTING AND RESULTS';H '5.1 Testing Strategy' 2;T 'Testing claims must match evidence. The repository contains typecheck-output.txt and build/prebuild logs, so static/source-level validation can be discussed. No supplied emulator recording, Firebase console proof, automated test suite, device matrix or multi-user trace supports claims about deployed behavior. The strategy separates code inspection from recommended runtime tests.';H '5.2 Testing Environment' 2;T 'Configuration indicates TypeScript, React Native, Expo and Android native tooling. package.json requires Node version 20 or later, but earlier than 23. Exact emulator/device, Android API level, Firebase environment and network conditions were not documented as verified conditions.';H '5.3 Classification' 2;T 'Verified: supplied source/configuration and typecheck output. Not verified: live authentication, Firestore operations, rules decisions, cross-device synchronization and DND device effect.' }
Page {H '5.4 Source-Level Test Cases' 2;Grid @('ID','Check','Expected / evidence') @(@('TC-01','TypeScript record','Supplied typecheck output inspected'),@('TC-02','Auth routing','Conditional route code inspected'),@('TC-03','Todo creation','addTodo document fields inspected'),@('TC-04','Focus accumulation','Transaction and 80% threshold inspected'),@('TC-05','Session lifecycle','start/cancel/complete functions inspected'),@('TC-06','Group access','join/request functions inspected'),@('TC-07','Chat','send/subscription functions inspected'));T 'These are code-inspection tests, not execution logs. “Inspected” means that the relevant code path was present and readable in the supplied repository.' 3 10 $false 0|Out-Null }
Page {H '5.5 Runtime Test Cases Required (Not Claimed as Passed)' 2;Grid @('ID','Scenario','Expected result','Status') @(@('RT-01','Email/password sign-in','Authenticated routing','Not evidenced'),@('RT-02','Google sign-in','Firebase user','Not evidenced'),@('RT-03','Todo and reload','Subscribed UI update','Not evidenced'),@('RT-04','Focus start/stop','Session/totals update','Not evidenced'),@('RT-05','Private request approval','Membership created','Not evidenced'),@('RT-06','Two-device chat','Message shared','Not evidenced'),@('RT-07','Attendance threshold','Presence update','Not evidenced'),@('RT-08','Android DND','Permission/effect','Not evidenced'));T 'Future execution should use test accounts and a non-production Firebase project, retain logs/screenshots and replace statuses only with observed results.' 3 10 $false 0|Out-Null }
Page {H '5.6 Actual Verified Results and Limitations' 2;Grid @('Area','Verified statement / limitation') @(@('Compilation','A supplied typecheck output records a TypeScript result.'),@('Source structure','Files/functions described in Chapters 3–4 were inspected.'),@('Screenshots','Repository PNG assets are embedded; backend context unknown.'),@('Firebase','Config/SDK present; live credentials/rules/network untested.'),@('Android build','Gradle project/logs exist; clean installation not claimed.'),@('Performance','No latency, battery, load or scalability measurements.'),@('Security','No rules or security-audit artefact supplied.'));H '5.7 Interpretation' 2;T 'Samay is a substantially implemented client codebase with coherent modules. Operational success remains dependent on configuration and runtime validation. This conclusion is more defensible than extrapolating execution from the presence of code.' }
Page {H 'CHAPTER 6: CONCLUSION AND FUTURE SCOPE';H '6.1 Project Summary' 2;T 'Samay unifies study planning, focus timing, session tracking, calendar/statistics views and study-group collaboration. Its TypeScript React Native structure separates screens, hooks, services, types and contexts. Firebase supplies identity/cloud documents; AsyncStorage preserves selected local state; an Android DND pathway is included.';H '6.2 Objectives Achieved' 2;T 'At source level, the objectives are addressed: authentication-aware routing, profile handling, focus lifecycle, todo CRUD and focus association, calendar/statistics retrieval, group roles, chat, attendance and leaderboards. This report preserves the distinction between code implementation and unverified runtime outcomes.' }
Page {H '6.3 Limitations and Future Enhancements' 2;Grid @('Area','Limitation','Future work') @(@('Validation','No end-to-end evidence','Scripted device/backend tests'),@('Security','Rules unavailable','Document rules and role tests'),@('Offline','Selected local state only','Queue/conflict design'),@('Testing','No formal suite','Mocks, hook tests and E2E'),@('Accessibility','No audit artefact','Labels, contrast and scaling audit'),@('CamStudy','Coming soon','Consent/privacy-first design'),@('Analytics','Basic summaries','Transparent goal/trend insights'));H '6.4 Final Conclusion' 2;T 'Samay provides a credible technical foundation for integrated study productivity and group collaboration. The next milestone is systematic runtime validation, backend-rule documentation and evidence-based usability evaluation.' }

